cribe.\n- [ ] Unsubscribe stops notifications.\n- [ ] `cancel(id)` on pending removes from queue (not returned afterward).\n- [ ] `cancel(id)` on processing sets `cancelled` and frees slot.\n- [ ] Cancelled task never retried even with retries remaining.\n\n## Phase 10 — Recurring Tasks\n- [ ] `schedule(cron, queue, payload, opts?)` returns an id; supports `*/N * * * *`, `0 * * * *`, `0 0 * * *`.\n- [ ] `listSchedules()` / `removeSchedule(id)` work; removal stops occurrences.\n- [ ] `tick(now?)` enqueues tasks for due schedules.\n- [ ] Enqueued recurring tasks behave like normal tasks.\n\n## Phase 11 — Middleware Pipeline\n- [ ] `use(queue, mw)` registers middleware; `setHandler(queue, fn)` registers handler.\n- [ ] `process(queue)` runs task through middleware in order, then handler.\n- [ ] Not calling `next` skips remaining pipeline + handler.\n- [ ] Middleware can mutate the task/payload.\n- [ ] Middleware throw → task failed (subject to retry).\n- [ ] Each queue has independent middleware stack.\n\n## Phase 12 — Graceful Shutdown\n- [ ] `shutdown({ timeout })` stops accepting tasks; later `add` throws.\n- [ ] Waits for processing tasks up to timeout.\n- [ ] On timeout, remaining processing tasks force-cancelled.\n- [ ] `onShutdown(cb)` callbacks run during shutdown.\n- [ ] Summary: `{ completed, forceCancelled, durationMs }`.\n- [ ] Idempotent: repeat calls return same result.\n- [ ] No processing tasks → completes immediately.\n\n## Global\n- [ ] `npm run build` compiles clean.\n- [ ] `npm run lint` passes.\n- [ ] `npm test` all green.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
