+# CONTRACT — In-Memory Task Queue
+
+Definition of done. Every box must be verified by a test in `src/__tests__/`.
+
+## Phase 1 — Basic FIFO Queue
+- [ ] `add(payload)` returns a task with unique `id`, `status==='pending'`, numeric `createdAt`.
+- [ ] Two adds produce different ids.
+- [ ] `getNext()` returns oldest pending task and sets its status to `processing`.
+- [ ] `getNext()` returns `null` when nothing is pending.
+- [ ] Tasks are returned in FIFO order.
+- [ ] `size()` reports how many tasks are waiting; decreases after `getNext`.
+
+## Phase 2 — Named Queues
+- [ ] `add(payload, { queue: 'a' })` puts task in queue `a`; default queue used when omitted.
+- [ ] Queues are independent: adding to `a` does not change `b`'s size.
+- [ ] `getNext('a')` pulls only from `a`.
+- [ ] `listQueues()` lists existing queue names.
+- [ ] `getNext` on non-existent/empty queue returns `null`.
+- [ ] Phase-1 calls (no queue name) still work via `default`.
+
+## Phase 3 — Priority
+- [ ] `priority` defaults to 5; exposed on task.
+- [ ] Lower number = higher priority returned first.
+- [ ] Equal priority preserves FIFO.
+- [ ] priority < 1 or > 10 throws.
+- [ ] Priority ordering is per-queue.
+
+## Phase 4 — Delayed / Scheduled
+- [ ] `delay` (ms) defers availability; task not returned before `availableAt`.
+- [ ] `runAt` (timestamp/Date) sets absolute availability.
+- [ ] Non-delayed tasks preferred over not-yet-available delayed tasks.
+- [ ] Among delayed-now-available: ordered by availableAt, then priority, then FIFO.
+- [ ] `availableAt` exposed on task.
+- [ ] Delays work per named queue.
+
+## Phase 5 — Retry with Backoff
+- [ ] `complete(id)` marks a processing task `completed`.
+- [ ] `fail(id)` on a task with retries left re-queues it with delay `backoffBase * 2^(attempt-1)`.
+- [ ] `maxRetries` default 3, configurable per task.
+- [ ] `backoffBase` default 1000, configurable per task.
+- [ ] `attempts` increments each time the task is retrieved.
+- [ ] Retried task keeps queue and priority.
+- [ ] After retries exhausted the task ends in `failed` state.
+
+## Phase 6 — Dead Letter Queue
+- [ ] Task with no retries left is moved to its queue's DLQ.
+- [ ] `getDeadLetters(queue)` lists dead-lettered tasks with error + attempt count.
+- [ ] `retryDeadLetter(id)` moves it back to original queue for fresh retries.
+- [ ] `clearDeadLetters(queue)` empties the DLQ.
+- [ ] Each queue has an independent DLQ.
+
+## Phase 7 — Dependencies
+- [ ] `dependencies: string[]` blocks a task until all complete.
+- [ ] Blocked tasks are not returned by `getNext`.
+- [ ] Completing a dependency unblocks dependents.
+- [ ] Circular dependency rejected at creation.
+- [ ] Depending on non-existent task throws.
+- [ ] Failed dependency leaves dependents blocked (not auto-failed).
+- [ ] `getDependencyStatus(id)` reports satisfied/unsatisfied deps.
+
+## Phase 8 — Concurrency Control
+- [ ] `setConcurrency(queue, n)` limits simultaneous processing.
+- [ ] At limit, `getNext` returns `null` even with pending tasks.
+- [ ] `complete`/`fail`/`cancel` free a slot.
+- [ ] Default concurrency unlimited.
+- [ ] `getConcurrency(queue)` and `getActiveCount(queue)` query state.
+- [ ] Highest-priority task still chosen subject to limit.
+
+## Phase 9 — Progress & Cancellation
+- [ ] `updateProgress(id, pct, msg?)` on a processing task; pct 0-100 validated.
+- [ ] `getProgress(id)` returns current progress.
+- [ ] `onProgress(id, cb)` notified on change; returns unsubscribe.
+- [ ] Unsubscribe stops notifications.
+- [ ] `cancel(id)` on pending removes from queue (not returned afterward).
+- [ ] `cancel(id)` on processing sets `cancelled` and frees slot.
+- [ ] Cancelled task never retried even with retries remaining.
+
+## Phase 10 — Recurring Tasks
+- [ ] `schedule(cron, queue, payload, opts?)` returns an id; supports `*/N * * * *`, `0 * * * *`, `0 0 * * *`.
+- [ ] `listSchedules()` / `removeSchedule(id)` work; removal stops occurrences.
+- [ ] `tick(now?)` enqueues tasks for due schedules.
+- [ ] Enqueued recurring tasks behave like normal tasks.
+
+## Phase 11 — Middleware Pipeline
+- [ ] `use(queue, mw)` registers middleware; `setHandler(queue, fn)` registers handler.
+- [ ] `process(queue)` runs task through middleware in order, then handler.
+- [ ] Not calling `next` skips remaining pipeline + handler.
+- [ ] Middleware can mutate the task/payload.
+- [ ] Middleware throw → task failed (subject to retry).
+- [ ] Each queue has independent middleware stack.
+
+## Phase 12 — Graceful Shutdown
+- [ ] `shutdown({ timeout })` stops accepting tasks; later `add` throws.
+- [ ] Waits for processing tasks up to timeout.
+- [ ] On timeout, remaining processing tasks force-cancelled.
+- [ ] `onShutdown(cb)` callbacks run during shutdown.
+- [ ] Summary: `{ completed, forceCancelled, durationMs }`.
+- [ ] Idempotent: repeat calls return same result.
+- [ ] No processing tasks → completes immediately.
+
+## Global
+- [ ] `npm run build` compiles clean.
+- [ ] `npm run lint` passes.
+- [ ] `npm test` all green.
